== e2  2026-11-17  train: "thyroidectomy" 45 s  |  thinking off, 3 assets, 7 shots, 2 director rounds  |  12 min, 63 calls, 151k out  |  BASELINE (user: "this is good")
score: look 3, motion 3, staging 3, readability 3, story 3, length 5 (47.6 s of 45)
flaws:
- hero recognisable now (two lobes + bridge) but wrong anatomy in the plan's description (bridge high, lobes wide at top): M3's memory is wrong, and an M3 fact-check repeated the same error
- hero too small in some shots and in the top half in others; band above the caption empty
- invented commentary labels ("AIRWAY INTACT", "NERVE PROTECTED", "THYROID REGION MARKED", "RLN + ...")
- hook is a definition again; invented "marks the tissue" step again; outcome beat dropped again (all three were already prose rules: M3 skipped them)
- white flash at every cut (host transition); all 3 asset craft passes rejected as "not deterministic" (validator false alarm from leaked canvas state)
lesson: prose rules M3 skips must become checks that reject with a measured number
fixes (system, not the reel):
- engine: reference step (M3 names 1-3 Wikipedia articles, engine fetches their text; plan and director must agree with it); hook-not-definition check; template "## checks" section (beats, required beats, hero width, hero centre y, labels); every shot carries a "beat"; craft pass gets one repair try when its improvement is rejected
- stage: shot check for hero drawn width and centre y at payoff (measured from drawn pixels, not the declared box); labels may only use words this shot's narration says; crash messages give the exact code line and a hint; asset validator resets canvas state between test draws; no white flash at cuts
- template: beat names on the structure; hero listed first; hero centre y 850-1000; checks section
- _base: REFERENCE wins over memory; silhouettes stated with the reference's numbers
next: e3 (train) and jet-engine-t1 (held-out test) run in parallel

