== t1  2026-11-17  TEST (held out): "how a jet engine works" 45 s  |  same run conditions  |  23 min, 82 calls, 1.06M tokens, $0.394
score: look 3, motion 3, staging 2, readability 4, story 3, length 2 (36.1 s)
result: template generalises: clear turbofan cutaway (fan, compressor, combustor, turbine, nozzle), labels on the right parts, step badges, same look. Flaws shared with e3: rectangle behind the context asset; wide subject leaves the lower band empty; reel short (speech-rate bug)
cost: review rounds are 59-65% of each reel's cost; craft passes 42-48% (a third of that was craft on director revisions)
fixes (system):
- stage: fresh canvas state every frame (unbalanced save leaked zoom into the next frame and compounded); save/restore count check in shots and assets; assets may not paint their whole box (corners must stay empty); validation pages use a CPU canvas (Chrome switched GPU->CPU after a few readbacks mid-validation: that anti-aliasing change was every "not deterministic" craft rejection); video render keeps the 2.3x faster GPU canvas
- engine: speech rate 2.7 words/s (measured 2.5-2.9; 2.1 made reels 10 s short); no craft pass on director revisions; hook regex article optional; rejected craft code saved to the work dir; cost_report.mjs + <out>-cost.txt per reel (tokens and cost per phase, draft/fix/craft split)
open: wide subjects in a 9:16 frame leave an empty band (needs a placement rule for wide heroes); glows drawn as big ellipses
